#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:79
msgid "<!-- END TILE IR REQUIREMENTS -->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:81
msgid ""
"The if/select optimization-hints row describes acceptance in the frontend "
"IR. These hints are discarded when emitting 13.5 bytecode and have no "
"backend performance effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:85
msgid ""
"Requirements combine. For example, FP4 packing needs both the `pack/unpack` "
"operations and the FP4 element type. A Hopper target requires Tile IR 13.3 "
"even when the operations themselves were available earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:89
msgid ""
"Architecture numbers are not a feature hierarchy: `sm_120` supports NVFP4, "
"but not scaled MMA using `f8E5M3FNU` scales. Operand types, shapes and "
"attribute values still have to satisfy the operation's verifier. In "
"particular, `num_worker_warps_per_cta` accepts 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 or 32 in 13.3 "
"and 13.5, and only 4 or 8 in 13.4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:95
msgid ""
"PDL additionally needs the driver's `cuLaunchKernelEx` entry point. Optional "
"host APIs are resolved at runtime; their availability is separate from the "
"device IR requirements. See the [PDL launch contract](host-"
"api.md#programmatic-dependent-launch)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:99
msgid ""
"The driver/toolkit combination must meet [NVIDIA's CUDA compatibility rules]"
"(https://docs.nvidia.com/deploy/cuda-compatibility/minor-version-"
"compatibility.html). We do not impose a blanket driver-version-at-least-"
"toolkit-version check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:103
msgid "CUDA 13.5 features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:105
msgid ""
"The 13.5 surface includes unicast/multicast pointer classification, "
"`multimem_load_reduce_view_tko`, `multimem_reduce_view_tko`, "
"`multimem_store_view_tko`, atomic-view inbounds promises, TMA validity "
"checking, minimum residency hints, and function argument attributes. The "
"named `simt` preview is separate from this stable surface. cuTile Rust "
"supports [foreign tile-library calls](../guide/tile-libraries.md) through "
"that preview; see the guide for the supported operands and current "
"limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:113
msgid ""
"The raw Rust APIs are exposed as unsafe functions in `cutile::tileir`, "
"defined in `cutile/src/_tileir.rs`: `ptr_with_attr_unicast`, "
"`ptr_with_attr_multicast`, the three `multimem_*_view_tko` operations, "
"`atomic_red_view_tko_with_inbounds`, and `load_view_tko_valid_check`. The "
"`multimem` module provides Add, Min, Max, And, Or, Xor, Umin, and Umax "
"reduction markers. These unsafe APIs require live, correctly classified "
"mappings and an explicit memory-ordering protocol. A Tile IR token does not "
"synchronize independent GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:121
msgid ""
"See [Unsafe GPU communication](unsafe-comms.md) for unicast and multicast "
"contracts, available synchronization primitives, and the runnable two-GPU "
"example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:124
msgid ""
"Likelihood uses the safe `Likely` extension trait, imported by `use "
"cutile::core::*`. The receiver must be a scalar `bool` or a boolean `Tile`, "
"and the method preserves its type and value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:128
msgid ""
"if condition.likely::<true>() {\n"
"    // Ordinary control flow; the existing DSL restrictions still apply.\n"
"}\n"
"let result = select(mask.likely::<false>(), a, b);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:135
msgid ""
"The prediction is advisory: an incorrect hint never affects correctness. "
"Copies and inline helpers preserve the IR hint; boolean computations and "
"control-flow joins may discard it. Apply it to the final condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:139
msgid ""
"**Tile IR 13.5 discards likelihood hints during bytecode emission.** The "
"methods currently require 13.5 but have no backend performance effect on "
"that target. Ordinary `if` and `select` use the standard 13.5 encoding, "
"without an optimization-hints field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:144
msgid ""
"Entry annotations accept `optimization_hints = (sm_100 = (min_ctas_per_sm = "
"2,),)` and a `default` group. `CompileOptions::min_ctas_per_sm` overrides "
"the entry hint for the active GPU and participates in JIT cache identity. "
"Minimum residency is in the range 0–32; zero disables the constraint. Hints "
"do not change program semantics. Function argument attributes are available "
"through the low-level IR builder. `DISubprogram::is_declaration` exposes the "
"13.5 debug declaration flag; ordinary definitions keep the flag clear, and "
"older writers reject declarations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:153
msgid ""
"The named `simt` preview has its own feature gate and is not a versioned CTK "
"13.5 API; 13.6 MMA overflow attributes are also outside this versioned "
"surface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:156
msgid ""
"Multicast operations require an NVLink SHARP-capable fabric and the "
"supported `sm_100`, `sm_103`, or `sm_107` families. `valid_check=true` "
"specifically needs `sm_107` with TMA enabled; B200 does not cover this "
"feature. False validity checks and all-false atomic inbounds arrays retain "
"their older version floor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:161
msgid "Selecting the toolkit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:163
msgid ""
"Install a CUDA 13.5 toolkit for the host architecture and select its "
"assembler explicitly when the default environment uses an older toolkit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:166
msgid ""
"export CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH=/path/to/cuda-13.5\n"
"export CUTILE_TILEIRAS_PATH=\"$CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH/bin/tileiras\"\n"
"export CUTILE_BYTECODE_VERSION=13.5\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:172
msgid ""
"Use one toolkit installation across projects. The assembler and its compiler "
"backend must support the requested bytecode version; changing a runtime "
"library path does not upgrade the assembler. Tile libraries must be built "
"for the toolkit that links them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:177
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:179
msgid ""
"Run from `cutile-rs/`. The normal CPU runner includes the new frontend, "
"bytecode, validation, and GPU-kernel compilation tests. When a matching CUDA "
"Tile IR translator is available, the following also checks the emitted "
"images with its independent C++ bytecode reader and verifier:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:184
msgid ""
"CUTILE_REFERENCE_TRANSLATE=/path/to/cuda-tile-translate \\\n"
"  cargo test -p cutile --test tile_ir_13_5 --test tile_ir_13_5_multicast\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:189
msgid ""
"With the shared 13.5 environment above, assemble the feature and multicast "
"execution kernels without a GPU. The validity-check kernel targets `sm_107`; "
"the other kernels target `sm_100`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:193
msgid ""
"cargo test -p cutile --test tile_ir_13_5 --test tile_ir_13_5_multicast \\\n"
"  assemble_ -- --ignored\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:198
msgid "Then on the two-or-more-GPU B200 instance with NVLink SHARP:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:200
msgid ""
"cargo test -p cutile --test tile_ir_13_5_multicast \\\n"
"  multicast_load_reduce_and_store_execute_from_each_gpu -- --ignored --test-"
"threads=1\n"
"bash scripts/run_gpu_tests.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:206
msgid ""
"The dedicated multicast test exercises each GPU as initiator, checks the "
"load-reduced output and both devices' storage after reduction/store, and "
"fails if the required devices or fabric are absent. It is ignored by default "
"because single-GPU machines cannot run it. Assembler and hardware execution "
"remain separate from passing the CPU suite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:212
msgid "Keeping the tables current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:214
msgid ""
"Requirements live in `cutile-ir/src/requirements.rs`, based on the "
"[versioned Tile IR specification](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/tile-ir/13.4/"
"sections/stability.html). When changing them, print the README and reference "
"tables with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:218
msgid "cargo run -p cutile-ir --example feature_matrix\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/compatibility.md:222
msgid ""
"The `documented_matrices_match_the_registry` test checks both checked-in "
"tables. CPU tests exercise the requirements without a driver; assembler CI "
"covers 13.2, 13.3, and 13.4. See the [Tile workflow](https://github.com/"
"NVIDIA/cuda-rust/blob/main/.github/workflows/cutile-rs.yml) for the current "
"image pins and enabled jobs. Examples report unsupported prerequisites as "
"`SKIP`; discovery, compilation, and execution errors remain failures."
msgstr ""
